From 139c597e0c8055d9c57b4fd0a5e03012325a72dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bart Schilperoort <b.schilperoort@esciencecenter.nl>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:56:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] T5.1: engine switch

[solver] engine = "mf6" | "gpu" (default mf6), with backend, precision and
preconditioner ("auto") for the GPU engine. The GPU engine builds the model of
write_simulation in memory with ModflowGPU's builder (build_spec, no MF6 files),
runs it through ModflowGPU's stepping API, stores RCH rates per unit area (no
MF6 6.3 area scaling in calibrate_bmi!) and writes absolute river stages into
the RIV BOUND mirror (converted to offsets from GWF/HREF in Float64). The tests
run with both engines (MODFLOWCOUPLING_ENGINES), check build_spec against the
loaded MF6 input and the head parity of the two engines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
